This is the same procedure sawtooth and I use. He has pointed out to me
that doing step 3 before step 2 would save a bit of time (because "The
Heart of Ahriman" is a lot more to type than say "axf"). Though I just
noticed that you've labeled your steps incorrectly. :)

If you don't like abusing this bug, you can do the following (which
does generally take more than five turns):

1. Kick it. "Thump" equals loadstone - don't pick it up!
2. Rub it against something metal. "scritch scritch" equals touchstone.
3. Price ID it. If it sells for more than a zorkmid, then it's a
luckstone.
4. Otherwise it's flint.

